  "answer_text": "The **comic book** came first! Here's a quick breakdown:\n\n- **The Comic:** *The Walking Dead* was a monthly black-and-white American comic that started in **2003**, created and written by Robert Kirkman with artist Tony Moore. It is an American post-apocalyptic comic book series, and beginning in 2003, published by Image Comics, the series ran for 193 issues, with Kirkman unexpectedly ending the series in **2019**.\n\n- **The TV Show:** In January 2010, AMC ordered a pilot for *The Walking Dead*, based on the comic book of the same name and developed by Frank Darabont and Gale Anne Hurd. Andrew Lincoln was cast as Rick Grimes, and the show premiered on **October 31, 2010**.\n\nSo the comic predates the TV show by about **7 years**. The AMC television series loosely follows the storyline of the comic book.",
